        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The issue seems to be that plugin code uses `vim.api.nvim_list_uis()` to get information about instance dimensions ([here](https://github.com/shortcuts/no-neck-pain.nvim/blob/ecc584150f5c8a2a82f2e1d43201df0f65c63d0e/lua/no-neck-pain/state.lua#L589-L592), [here](https://github.com/shortcuts/no-neck-pain.nvim/blob/ecc584150f5c8a2a82f2e1d43201df0f65c63d0e/lua/no-neck-pain/wins.lua#L194), and [here](https://github.com/shortcuts/no-neck-pain.nvim/blob/ecc584150f5c8a2a82f2e1d43201df0f65c63d0e/lua/no-neck-pain/wins.lua#L216)). As tests now run in headless mode, it means that there are no UIs attached to them initially (that's basically what `:h --headless` says).\r\n\r\nMy personal recommendation would be to not use `nvim_list_uis()` if the only information you want is instance dimensions. Using `vim.o.columns` and `vim.o.lines` for width and height usually seems to be enough. Those work even in headless instance. I tried replacing those in code and it resulted in a several regular test failures. Those require some code base knowledge, so I stopped here.\r\n\r\nOther approaches are to updates tests to either mock `vim.api.nvim_list_uis()` or use `vim.api.nvim_ui_attach()`.\r\n\r\nClosing as an intended behavior of 'mini.test'.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nNotes:\r\n- The way I debugged this was to first notice that there is a visible delay in failing tests which usually indicate some kind of non-direct error shown in child process. Then I edited one of failing tests to include `Helpers.expect.equality(child.cmd_capture('messages'))` to see what messages were shown. It returned a `attempt to index a nil value` at ['no-neck-pain/state.lua:591'](https://github.com/shortcuts/no-neck-pain.nvim/blob/ecc584150f5c8a2a82f2e1d43201df0f65c63d0e/lua/no-neck-pain/state.lua#L591) with additional traceback. This pointed directly at `nvim_list_uis()` not behaving as you'd expect.\r\n- [Requiring plugin's module from running instance](https://github.com/shortcuts/no-neck-pain.nvim/blob/ecc584150f5c8a2a82f2e1d43201df0f65c63d0e/tests/test_API.lua#L1) means that the module must be visible which is not a very clean setup, as ideally the only place plugin should be loaded is child process.",
